{% liquid
  assign faq_items = "What exactly are these chews made of?|4 simple ingredients: yak milk, cow milk, lime juice, and salt. That is the full list. No rawhide, no fillers, no artificial color, and no mystery powders.||Where do they come from?|Our chews are made in Nepal using traditional Himalayan cheese methods, then checked and packed in the USA before shipping to you.||Are they actually natural?|Yes. The recipe is short on purpose: yak milk, cow milk, lime juice, and salt. What you see on the label is what is inside.||How long do they last?|It depends on your dog. Size, jaw strength, age, and chewing style all change the answer. Many dogs settle into a longer supervised session than they do with soft treats, but your first chew is the best reference point.||Do they smell bad or make a mess?|They are low odor compared with many animal chews. They are still a real dairy chew, but they should not leave greasy residue like some alternatives.||Are yak chews safe for my dog?|Yes, when sized correctly and supervised. Choose a chew larger than your dog can swallow whole, keep fresh water nearby, and take the chew away once the end gets small.||Can they break my dog's teeth?|Yak chews are hard by design, so they are not right for every dog. If your dog has weak teeth, dental disease, crowns, or a history of cracked teeth, ask your vet before using any hard chew.||What's the thumbnail test?|Press your thumbnail into the chew. If you cannot make a small indent, use extra caution for dogs with dental concerns. The test is useful, but sizing, supervision, and tooth health still matter.||Are they safe for puppies?|For puppies over 6 months with adult teeth coming in, start with a small size and supervise closely. For younger puppies still teething, we recommend waiting.||What about senior dogs?|Some senior dogs do well with yak chews, but dental health matters most. If your senior dog has missing teeth, dental disease, or a sensitive mouth, ask your vet first.||What if my dog swallows a piece?|Small pieces are usually easier to digest because the chew is cheese-based. If your dog swallows a large chunk or seems uncomfortable, contact your vet. Remove the chew before it becomes a swallowable nub.||How often can I give my dog a yak chew?|Most families use one a few times per week for evening wind-downs, work calls, or supervised quiet time. Treat it like any chew: use moderation and keep water nearby.||How long do they actually last per session?|Your dog sets the pace. Light chewers may use one over several sessions. Strong chewers move faster. The chew duration estimator can help you choose a practical starting size.||What's the Nub Hack?|When the chew gets down to about 2 inches, take it away. Soak it in water, microwave it until it puffs, then let it cool completely before serving.||How do I choose the right size?|Match by weight and chewing style. When your dog is between sizes, choose the larger chew. A slightly larger chew is usually easier to manage safely than one that is too small.||How fast do orders ship?|Most orders ship within 1-2 business days and arrive in 3-5 business days through USPS or UPS. Free shipping is available on orders over $30.||What's your return policy?|We have a 30-day promise. If the size or routine is not right, reach out and we will help with the next best step.||Can I change or cancel my subscription?|Yes. Skip a month, change delivery timing, swap sizes, or cancel from your account page. No hidden commitment.||How does Subscribe and Save work?|Choose your chew size and delivery rhythm. Your future orders ship automatically on the schedule you choose, and you can adjust it when your dog's routine changes.||Why is Prime Pet Food different from other yak chews?|Our founder grew up with this food tradition in Nepal, the recipe is short, and our team helps with sizing and safety instead of just selling a bag." | split: "||"
%}

<section class="prime-faq-page" aria-labelledby="PrimeFaqTitle">
  <div class="pfq-shell">
    <header class="pfq-hero">
      <p class="pfq-kicker">Questions we actually get asked</p>
      <h1 id="PrimeFaqTitle">Everything you want to know before the first chew.</h1>
      <p>
        Sizing, safety, ingredients, shipping, subscriptions. We answer these every day — here they are in one place.
      </p>
      <div class="pfq-actions" aria-label="FAQ actions">
        <a href="/pages/how-long-will-this-last-for-my-dog" class="pfq-button pfq-button--primary">Find your dog's size</a>
        <a href="/pages/subscribe-and-save" class="pfq-button pfq-button--secondary">Subscribe &amp; Save</a>
        <a href="/pages/contact" class="pfq-button pfq-button--secondary">Ask us anything</a>
      </div>
      <div class="pfq-search">
        <label for="PrimeFaqSearch">Search questions</label>
        <input id="PrimeFaqSearch" type="search" placeholder="Try: puppy, size, shipping, ingredients..." autocomplete="off">
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="pfq-layout">
      <aside class="pfq-sidebar" aria-label="FAQ categories">
        <a href="#product">Product</a>
        <a href="#safety">Safety</a>
        <a href="#duration">Duration</a>
        <a href="#sizing">Sizing</a>
        <a href="#orders">Orders</a>
        <a href="#subscriptions">Subscribe &amp; Save</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="pfq-content">
        <section class="pfq-category" id="product">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Product & ingredients</p>
          {% for item in faq_items limit: 5 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item" {% if forloop.first %}open{% endif %}>
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="safety">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Safety & digestion</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 5 limit: 8 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div>
                <p>{{ parts[1] }}</p>
                <p class="pfq-related">
                  {% case parts[0] %}
                    {% when 'Are yak chews safe for dogs?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chew-safety-guide">Read the yak chew safety guide</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/how-long-will-this-last-for-my-dog">Use the size estimator</a>
                    {% when 'Are yak chews better than rawhide?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/best-rawhide-alternative">Compare rawhide alternatives</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/natural-dog-chews">Explore natural dog chews</a>
                    {% when 'Can puppies eat yak chews?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chews-for-puppies">Read the puppy yak chew guide</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chew-safety-guide">Review safety basics</a>
                    {% when 'What if my dog swallows a small piece?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chew-safety-guide">Read small-piece safety guidance</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/contact">Contact support</a>
                    {% when 'How often should I give a yak chew?' %}
                      <a href="/pages/are-yak-chews-digestible">Read the digestibility guide</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/pages/how-long-do-yak-chews-last">Plan chew duration</a>
                    {% else %}
                      <a href="/pages/yak-chew-safety-guide">Read the safety guide</a>
                      <span>·</span>
                      <a href="/collections/all">Shop by size</a>
                  {% endcase %}
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="duration">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Chew duration & routine</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 13 limit: 2 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="sizing">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Sizing & recommendations</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 15 limit: 1 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="orders">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Shipping & support</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 16 limit: 3 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>

        <section class="pfq-category" id="subscriptions">
          <p class="pfq-category__label">Subscribe & Save</p>
          {% for item in faq_items offset: 19 %}
            {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
            <details class="pfq-item">
              <summary>{{ parts[0] }}</summary>
              <div><p>{{ parts[1] }}</p></div>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pfq-support">
      <div>
        <p class="pfq-kicker">Still not sure?</p>
        <h2>Just ask us directly.</h2>
        <p>Send your dog's breed, weight, age, and chewing style. We'll point you to the right size. We reply Monday–Friday, usually within a few hours.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/pages/contact" class="pfq-button pfq-button--primary">Send us a message</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {% for item in faq_items %}
      {% assign parts = item | split: "|" %}
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": {{ parts[0] | json }},
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": {{ parts[1] | strip_html | json }}
        }
      }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {% endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>

<script>
  (function() {
    var input = document.getElementById('PrimeFaqSearch');
    if (!input) return;
    var items = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.pfq-item'));
    var categories = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.pfq-category'));

    input.addEventListener('input', function() {
      var query = input.value.trim().toLowerCase();
      items.forEach(function(item) {
        var text = item.textContent.toLowerCase();
        var match = !query || text.indexOf(query) !== -1;
        item.hidden = !match;
        if (match && query) item.open = true;
      });
      categories.forEach(function(category) {
        var visible = category.querySelector('.pfq-item:not([hidden])');
        category.hidden = !visible;
      });
    });

    items.forEach(function(item, index) {
      var answer = item.querySelector('div');
      if (!answer || answer.querySelector('.pfq-helpful')) return;

      var helpful = document.createElement('div');
      helpful.className = 'pfq-helpful';
      helpful.innerHTML = '<span>Was this helpful?</span><button type="button" data-helpful="yes">Yes</button><button type="button" data-helpful="no">No</button>';
      answer.appendChild(helpful);

      helpful.addEventListener('click', function(event) {
        var button = event.target.closest('button');
        if (!button) return;
        helpful.dataset.selected = button.dataset.helpful;
        helpful.setAttribute('aria-label', button.dataset.helpful === 'yes' ? 'Marked helpful' : 'Marked not helpful');
      });
    });
  })();
</script>

